course: dictionary
lesson: 5683
title: Local: near home and local people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Local means belonging to or near the place where you live, or a particular area. Your local library, park and shop are the ones close to home. «Local words belong to real dialects», which means some words are only used in one area.
explain: The locals are the people who live in a place. «Ask a local» means ask someone who lives there, because they know it best. Local customs are the ways of doing things in one particular place, and visitors respect them.
explain: Local can have other meanings, so check the sentence. In Britain, «the local» can mean the nearby pub. In medicine, a local anaesthetic numbs only one part of the body. The words around the word tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Local means belonging to or near the place where you live, or a particular area.
fact: The locals are the people who live in a place.
fact: In Britain, «the local» can mean the nearby pub.
fact: Local customs are the ways of a particular place, and visitors respect them.
fact: «Dreich» means dull, grey and drizzly in Scotland, and «y'all» means you all in the southern US.
exercise: What does local mean in «the local library»? | *Close by, in the place where you live | Very large and famous | Far away across the sea | Old and falling down
exercise: In «The locals are kind to visitors», who are the locals? | The shopkeepers only | The people who are visiting | The police officers | *The people who live in the place
exercise: What is a local custom? | *A way of doing things that belongs to one particular place | A type of shoe | A very old castle | A kind of train ticket
test: In Britain, if someone says «Let's meet at the local», where are they going? | A church in the next town | A bus station | A big shopping centre | *A nearby pub
test: In medicine, what does a local anaesthetic do? | It makes you very hungry | It cures a cold | It puts the whole body to sleep | *It numbs only one part of the body
exam: Using the clue in «Local words belong to real dialects», what does local mean there? | *Belonging to one particular area | Very loud | Made of stone | Written down on paper
